# Rust
# The Cargo workspace root is the repo root, so build output lands in /target.
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# The compiled Rust extension, dropped into the package by `maturin develop`.
# Rebuild it with `maturin develop --release`; never commit it.
*.so
*.pyd
*.dylib

# Training artifacts. A run is reproducible from its config and its seed, so the shards and
# the per-generation checkpoints are not worth their weight in git.
# /models/ is the deliberate exception: the one checkpoint per run worth publishing is copied
# there by hand and tracked, so a clone can play the agent without training one. Keep any
# future *.d52nn rule out of this block, or it will swallow models/ too.
/runs/
/checkpoints/
*.pt
*.ckpt
/data/
/replay_buffers/

# The analysis corpora: the raw per-game and per-card CSVs `duel52 analyze` writes. Hours of
# play at a thousand simulations, but reproducible from the agent, the seed range and the
# rules hash, all of which are in the meta.json beside them. The **documents** built from
# them — analysis/<variant>.md and .html — are tracked, because those are the deliverable.
/analysis/*/

# Logs and profiling
*.log
/wandb/
/tensorboard/

# Working notes. Read-and-argue-with documents that nothing is held to; the tracked docs are
# PLAN.md, FINDINGS.md, game_rules.md and README.md.
/ALGORITHM_EXPLANATION.md

# macOS
.DS_Store
